§ `Tests -- section 525: review of detention where the trial is delayed`
-- the day the 90 days run from. args: the day taken before a justice under s 503; an order or a review decision exists; the day taken into custody under that order; the day of the decision
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the day from which the 90 days are counted` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the day from which the 90 days are counted` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) EQUALS Date 5 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the day from which the 90 days are counted` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) EQUALS Date 10 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the day from which the 90 days are counted` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) EQUALS Date 5 2 2026
-- the 90 days. 1 January 2026 is day 0 and 1 April 2026 is day 90 (31 + 28 + 31 = 90). args: the day counted from; the trial has commenced; the day it commenced; the day in question
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the trial has not commenced within 90 days from the day` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the trial has not commenced within 90 days from the day` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the trial has not commenced within 90 days from the day` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the trial has not commenced within 90 days from the day` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 5 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the trial has not commenced within 90 days from the day` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 2 4 2026) (Date 5 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the trial has not commenced within 90 days from the day` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 5 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1.1) waiver. args: the accused waived in writing; the judge received the waiver before the 90 days expired
#ASSERT `s 525(1.1) the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 525(1.1) the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1.1) the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1.1) the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) the duty. args: s 469; detained in custody pending trial for that offence; required to be detained in respect of another matter; the trial has not commenced within 90 days; not required under (1.1)
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` NOTHING TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a definite no from another gate beats a section 469 answer that is not covered
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the time of the application. args: the day counted from; the day the application was made; the application was made immediately after the expiry
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the application is made immediately after the expiry of those 90 days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the application is made immediately after the expiry of those 90 days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the application is made immediately after the expiry of those 90 days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the application is made immediately after the expiry of those 90 days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 525(1) the application is made immediately after the expiry of those 90 days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the duty as a regulative rule (a DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT on the stable binary; these are traces; the clock is in days from the expiry of the 90 days)
-- the person applies at once (FULFILLED); the person does not apply (the duty stays open: the text gives no deadline in days and no breach); the duty does not arise (FULFILLED)
#TRACE `s 525(1) the duty to apply` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused` DOES `s 525(1) apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` AT 0
#TRACE `s 525(1) the duty to apply` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)
#TRACE `s 525(1) the duty to apply` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)
-- (2)(a) the date: arg: the judge receives an application under (1)
#ASSERT `s 525(2)(a) the judge must fix a date for the hearing described in subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 525(2)(a) the judge must fix a date for the hearing described in subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(a)(i), (ii) args: the hearing is in the jurisdiction where the accused is in custody; where the trial is to take place
#ASSERT `s 525(2)(a) the place of the hearing is one the paragraph names` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 525(2)(a) the place of the hearing is one the paragraph names` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 525(2)(a) the place of the hearing is one the paragraph names` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
